# Trivy CVE exceptions for orkyo-foundation
#
# Format:
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN  # Impact | Reason | Added: YYYY-MM-DD | Review: YYYY-MM-DD
#
# Policy: time-bound only. Review date must be within 14 days of added date.
# Remove entries once the upstream fix is available.
#
# Reviewed 2026-10-01: The 26.7.5 pin cleared five vulnerable-library exceptions:
# Bouncy Castle (1.86), netty (4.1.138), FreeMarker (2.3.35), and Jackson (2.21.7).
# Jackson also closed CVE-2026-91776/91777, published 2026-10-01. The `mssql-jdbc`
# false-positive exception remains. Git history contains the review narrative.

# ── Trivy false positive ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Renewed on a 14-day cadence while it stays a false positive; a permanent-exception
# class (VEX) would end the churn — see the base-image-scan follow-ups.
CVE-2025-59250  # HIGH | mssql-jdbc: improper input validation — Trivy compares the installed 13.2.1 against a fix list ending 13.2.1.jre11 and calls it older; the shipped JAR is the fixed version, false positive (re-verified 2026-10-01 on quay.io/keycloak/keycloak:26.7.5, which still pins 13.2.1.jre11) | Added: 2026-10-01 | Review: 2026-10-15
